{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TopologicalMassFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TopologicalMassFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.archimedeanMass_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.archimedeanMass_pos","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula.lean#L83-L89","doc":"The archimedean mass is positive for hyperbolic knots (Vol > 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ArchimedeanMassFormula","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula.lean#L49-L81","doc":"**Archimedean Mass Formula** (Proposition):\n\nLet (C, A, τ) be the C-quantum observable universe and let K be a\nhyperbolic knot. The descent involution induces the idempotent\nsplitting End_C(A_{n+1}) = A^desc ⊕ A^trans. Under the archimedean\nfibre functor:\n- The descended trace evaluates to Hol_{∇_A} (the holonomy)\n- Each transient trace evaluates to Φ_q(z_i) (quantum dilogarithm)\n\nSumming: m(K) = Vol(K) + Vol(K)(1/ℏ_q² - 1) = Vol(K)/ℏ_q².\n\nThe derivation proceeds via three identifications from the categorical\ndecomposition (topological mass theorem):\n1. Baseline holonomy → Vol(K) via Chern-Simons/volume correspondence\n2. Exceptional divisor contributions → Vol(K) · (1/ℏ_q² - 1)\n3. Total: m = Vol(K)/ℏ_q² ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:topological-mass-formula","label":"prop:topological-mass-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.archimedeanMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.archimedeanMass","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula.lean#L45-L47","doc":"The archimedean mass formula: m(K) = Vol(K) / ℏ_q². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.quantumPlanck_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.quantumPlanck_pos","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula.lean#L40-L43","doc":"ℏ_q is positive for q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.quantumPlanck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.quantumPlanck","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula.lean#L37-L38","doc":"The quantum Planck constant ℏ_q = (q - 1)/q = 1 - 1/q. ","signatureChunk":0}]}